From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: the desktop keeps winspool loaded

winspool loads the system's (CUPS) printers when it is first loaded, once
per session, marked by a named mutex that lives only while a process holds
it. Short programs that link winspool -- GIMP's ~130 plug-ins, through GTK --
each found it gone and asked CUPS again, about a second apiece: GIMP's first
start took over three minutes. The desktop loads winspool on a thread and
keeps it, as the spooler service would.
---
--- a/programs/explorer/desktop.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/desktop.c
@@ -2710,6 +2710,18 @@
     if (thread) CloseHandle( thread );
 }
 
+/* Stained Glass OS: winspool loads the system's (CUPS) printers when it is
+ * first loaded, once per session -- a named mutex says it was done, and the
+ * mutex lives as long as some process holds it. Programs that link winspool
+ * and run briefly (GIMP starts some 130 plug-ins on its first run, each
+ * linking it through GTK) found it gone and asked CUPS again, a second each.
+ * The desktop keeps it loaded, as the spooler service would. */
+static DWORD WINAPI spooler_thread( void *arg )
+{
+    LoadLibraryW( L"winspool.drv" );
+    return 0;
+}
+
 static void set_desktop_window_title( HWND hwnd, const WCHAR *name )
 {
     static const WCHAR desktop_name_separatorW[] = L" - ";
@@ -2882,6 +2894,8 @@
                       SWP_SHOWWINDOW );
         thread = CreateThread( NULL, 0, clipboard_thread, NULL, 0, &id );
         if (thread) CloseHandle( thread );
+        thread = CreateThread( NULL, 0, spooler_thread, NULL, 0, NULL );
+        if (thread) CloseHandle( thread );
         SystemParametersInfoW( SPI_SETDESKWALLPAPER, 0, NULL, FALSE );
         ClipCursor( NULL );
         initialize_display_settings( width, height );
